## One-line revision

**Checkbox allows multiple selections, Radio allows one selection from a group, and Switch represents an ON/OFF setting.**


Dynamic Checkbox
List<String> skills = [
  "Flutter",
  "Python",
  "SQL",
  "Java",
];

Map<String, bool> selectedSkills = {};

Column(
  children: skills.map((skill) {
    return CheckboxListTile(
      title: Text(skill),
      value: selectedSkills[skill] ?? false,
      onChanged: (value) {
        setState(() {
          selectedSkills[skill] = value!;
        });
      },
    );
  }).toList(),
)



Dynamic RadioButton
List<String> genders = [
  "Male",
  "Female",
  "Other",
];

String selectedGender = "Male";

Column(
  children: genders.map((gender) {
    return RadioListTile<String>(
      title: Text(gender),
      value: gender,
      groupValue: selectedGender,
      onChanged: (value) {
        setState(() {
          selectedGender = value!;
        });
      },
    );
  }).toList(),
)